---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
---
<Base title="Review rules | RentalSpy" description="The rules for sharing rent and ratings on RentalSpy.">
  <Prose title="Review rules">
    <p class="lede">RentalSpy only works if people can trust it. These rules keep it honest and fair.</p>
    <h2>What you can share</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your own, real experience of a place you rent or rented.</li>
      <li>What you pay, the condition of the place, how repairs were handled, noise, and how a share house is kept.</li>
      <li>One short, practical tip for the next renter.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What's not allowed</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Names or details of any person</b>: tenants, housemates, landlords, agents or neighbours. Rate the place, not people.</li>
      <li>Accusations of crimes or illegal behaviour. If something illegal happened, contact the police or Consumer and Business Services instead.</li>
      <li>Phone numbers, emails, links or advertising.</li>
      <li>Places you haven't lived in, or more than one entry per address.</li>
      <li>Fake ratings, including by landlords, agents or their friends.</li>
      <li>Abuse, threats, or anything discriminatory.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How we keep it clean</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Written tips are checked before they appear.</li>
      <li>Anyone can report an entry. If 3 different people report it, it's hidden automatically until we look at it.</li>
      <li>We remove entries that break these rules. We don't remove honest entries just because someone dislikes them.</li>
      <li>Nobody can pay to change or remove a rating.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Rewards</h2>
    <p>If we ever run a prize draw or offer anything for sharing, it's given whether your rating is good or bad, and we say so on the page.</p>
    <p><a href="/report-a-problem/">Report a problem with an entry</a></p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
